Material source disclosure: part of the northern property is used by neighbouring land, potentially involving encroaching construction or use. Verify boundaries and actual occupation before offering.

SAM describes the title as a Chanot Tra Chong stamped as land already put to use. It reports no cadastral map sheet for locating this plot, with the parent or remaining parent title used to identify its position. SAM warns that location, dimensions, area and boundaries may differ from the depicted parcel. Verify title and actual boundaries with the Land Office; navigation coordinates do not certify boundaries.

According to SAM, title 1491 was issued on 6 October 1992, subdivided from parent title 15 issued in 1937, before the 1993 Royal Decree on the Navy military safety zone. SAM reports that enquiries to the Sattahip Land Office and Sattahip Naval Base real-estate division described evidence of possession predating that decree as lawful. This is attributed source information; buyers must verify current rights and conditions directly.

SAM further reports that the land remains within the royal reserved area under the 1922 Royal Command even where permission to occupy has been granted. Owners must submit documents to seek permission from the Sattahip Naval Base real-estate division. If permission conditions are later found unmet, the Navy may revoke permission and request the Land Department to revoke the land-rights document; SAM states that the occupant would have no right to contest or claim compensation. Obtain the plot-specific permission record, conditions and ownership-transfer procedure before deciding.

The trapezoidal plot has approximately 12 metres of western frontage and a maximum depth of 21.5 metres. Registered acquisition describes the three two-storey shophouses. Thet Saban 8 is described as public, with approximately 10 metres of concrete carriageway and a 12-metre right of way. SAM reports orange planning zoning.

From Ban Chang toward Bang Sare on Sukhumvit Road, turn left into Thet Saban 13 for approximately one kilometre, right into Thet Saban 10 for 180 metres, then right into Thet Saban 8 for 15.5 metres; the property is on the right.

SAM showed direct-purchase status and this price on 11 September 2026. Contact 02-686-1888, sales@sam.or.th or LINE @samline, quoting 8Z5730, to confirm availability, price, viewing, title, reserved-area permission, northern land use and terms.

